module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.behavior_named_edge_label_validated_not_constructed

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data behavior_named_edge_label_validated_not_constructed: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "behavior_named_edge_label_validated_not_constructed" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a behavior node carrying a Named edge whose label is not the marker that behavior admits -- a Transform with a Named edge other than `v2.std.type_binder` `<cast-target>`, or (once the let-annotation carrier lands) a Bind with a Named edge other than its annotation marker. `v2.std.node` states only the SHAPE (`PositionalPlusOneNamedEdges`: at most one Named edge beside the positional children) and cannot intern the marker lexemes, so the LABEL is checked by a second function, `v2.std.type_binder` `type_binder_labels_conform`, over any Node. HARM if it were not checked: a foreign Named edge on a Transform would be carried as a cast target nobody authored, or skipped by readers that pass the marker over.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: structurally guaranteed (rung 3), not impossible. The mislabelled node is CONSTRUCTIBLE -- Edge.label is an open `Named { name: Symbol }` -- but no Accepted program contains one: `v2.compiler.resolve` gates the tree on `well_formed(n) && type_binder_labels_conform(root: n)` before resolving, and refuses a mislabelled tree as malformed. Discriminating evidence: `v2.test.claim.body_cast_node` `bcn_a_foreign_label_on_a_transform_refuses` (a Transform carrying a non-marker Named edge fails the gate predicate) with its positive partner `bcn_a_loop_passes_the_resolver_gate` (a real fold-lowered Loop, whose Named edges belong to its own edge discipline, passes it); the Bind arm's control is `v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation` `bla_bind_admits_only_its_annotation_label` (a Bind carrying `<cast-target>` fails the gate, one carrying `<type-annotation>` passes), landed with the let-annotation carrier (gunbc#12322). Ruled by neat-boar-16 on review 71525 (gunbc#12322).",
    "CEILING: structurally impossible -- which label a behavior's Named edge may carry is decidable and fully modeled, so the invalid state need not have a constructor. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: edge labels on behavior nodes become a closed coproduct owned by `v2.std.node`, so a Transform's or Bind's Named edge can only be constructed as the marker that behavior admits and a foreign label has no constructor; `type_binder_labels_conform`'s label arm for behaviors then dissolves, its discriminating red kept as the evidence. It must be ONE authority with the edge-discipline coproduct gentle-koi-724's lane is building, not a second one beside it.",
    "THE WALL IS SPLIT, NOT WIDENED (MQ-1 PR-B, ruled by gentle-koi-724 and neat-boar-16, 2026-09-26; loyal-crab-333's wall). Named arguments now ride an application as Named edges labelled by the callee's parameter names (v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold body_lower_call_arg_edge), so a Transform is one of two forms: a cast, whose one Named edge is the <cast-target> marker, or an application, whose Named edges are named actuals. v2.std.node states a Transform's shape as positional_prefix_then_labeled_conform (positional first, then distinct Named edges -- an application's positional order carries meaning), while a Bind keeps PositionalPlusOneNamedEdges (one marker, placed freely) and admits only the <type-annotation> label (v2.std.type_binder bind_named_labels_conform), and v2.std.type_binder transform_named_labels_conform refuses a Transform that MIXES the marker with any other Named edge, located at that Transform (v2.std.type_binder type_binder_first_mislabelled, read by v2.compiler.resolve's gate). A named label that names no parameter of the callee is a binding fact, refused by the one binding authority (v2.std.arrow_signature application_binding_plan, application_argument_label_unknown) before any program is Accepted. So the rung stays structurally guaranteed, reached by two decidable halves instead of one label list. Discriminating reds: v2.test.claim.body_cast_node bcn_a_foreign_label_on_a_transform_refuses (restated as the mixing case) and bcn_an_unknown_named_label_refuses_at_binding; the cast controls in the same module are unchanged.",
    "WHAT THE TRIGGER MUST BE SUFFICIENT FOR, stated per DESIGN section 4b(3) (review 72087, MQ-1 PR-B). With named arguments, a Transform is one of two forms: a CAST whose one Named edge is the <cast-target> marker, or an APPLICATION whose Named edges are named actuals labelled by parameter names. v2.std.type_binder transform_named_labels_conform refuses a Transform that MIXES them -- validation over a state the model can still write, because the label is an open Named { name: Symbol }. A Cast behavior is not available (DESIGN section 4 fixes the six behaviors), so the construction route is this row's own trigger: behavior-node edge labels become a closed coproduct owned by v2.std.node. It is met only when that coproduct gives the cast marker and an application's named actual DISTINCT label constructors, so a marker beside an actual has no constructor; transform_named_labels_conform's mix arm then dissolves, and its discriminating red v2.test.claim.body_cast_node bcn_a_foreign_label_on_a_transform_refuses stays enrolled as the evidence (DESIGN section 4b(4)). Owner: the v2 type-binders lane under neat-boar-16, coordinated with the named-arguments edge discipline (v2.std.node positional_prefix_then_labeled_conform)."
    "CLIMB, EDGE LABELS (quiet-koi-814; model gunbc#12473, ruled by neat-boar-16, ruling A; scope ruled by gentle-koi-724). `v2.std.node` `EdgeLabel` is now `Authored { name } | StructuralLabel { label: StructuralEdgeLabel } | Positional`, with `StructuralEdgeLabel = CoreMarker { marker: CoreEdgeLabel } | ProductionEdge { language, edge }`; the old `Named { name: Symbol }` arm was deleted first and every site renamed or converted in one change (DESIGN section 3, root-first). CONVERTED, EVERY MINTER AND READER: the core markers (arrow body, arrow signature order, loop bound, carrier and domain, match arm pattern and body, the `v2.std.type_binder` cast target, type annotation, type params, type body and type alias, the declaration reference, the field projection base and field, and the construct tag from gunbc#12714) and the dag surface productions the text-matching readers needed (module header and its qualified name, where-refinement clause, import decl, import block, import decl block, import decl qualified name), plus `v2.std.node` `Path` steps and `v2.compiler.resolution_provenance` `ReferenceSite` position, which now carry whole labels. The four text-matching readers (`v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `dag_surface_module_header_metadata_edge` and the Absent-emission arm of `dag_node_is_module_root_conj`, `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_edge_names_where_clause`, `v2.lens.module_graph` `site_is_import_syntax_mention`) match the arm, so no Authored label reaches them whatever it spells. The marker lexemes (`<cast-target>` and siblings) are gone: a marker is an arm, not an unauthorable spelling.",
    "RUNG AFTER THE CLIMB, PER PATH. The confusion this row names -- a behavior's marker label read from an authored spelling -- is structurally impossible on every converted reader: an Authored value is never equal to a StructuralLabel value. What stays at rung 3 is the SHAPE half of the behavior rule: a Bind or a Transform can still be handed an Authored label where only its marker belongs (a Bind's only admitted label is its type annotation; a Transform's authored labels are its named actuals), so `type_binder_labels_conform` keeps refusing a foreign Authored label on a Bind and a cast marker mixed with named actuals. Its next-rung trigger is unchanged in kind: per-behavior label coproducts, so a Bind's named edge has no Authored constructor.",
    "DECLARED FRONTIER, AUTHORED ARM CARRYING GRAMMAR-EMITTED LABELS (ruled by gentle-koi-724 on the cut). Labels a grammar or a language model emits, but that no converted reader matches, still ride the Authored arm and their readers still compare text inside it. POPULATION, BY MINTING DECLARATION: the per-language edge builders `v2.extdeps.languages` `bash_named_edge`, `c_named_edge`, `c_decl_named_edge`, `cpp_named_edge`, `dag_named_edge` (its non-converted productions) and `dag_round_trip_edge`, `ecmascript_named_edge`, `english_named_edge`, `go_named_edge`, `java_named_edge`, `kotlin_named_edge`, `lean_named_edge`, `python_named_edge`, `rust_named_edge`, `swift_named_edge`, `swift_decl_named_edge`, `ts_named_edge`, `verilog_named_edge`, `wasm_named_edge`; the reflection builders `v2.std.compilers.target_model` `target_model_named_edge`, `v2.std.grammar` `grammar_named_edge` (including the four parse-projection labels `v2.compiler.parse` `parse_tree_projection_edge` rosters), `v2.std.fold_assembly` `named_edge`, `v2.std.integer` `integer_named_edge`, `v2.std.language_model` `language_model_named_edge`, `v2.std.logic` `bool_named_edge`, `v2.std.runtime` `runtime_value_named_edge`, `v2.std.node` `node_offset_named_edge`; and every caller of each. PREVIOUS RUNG: below the floor (one Symbol space). TEMPORARY RUNG: unchanged for this population -- an authored spelling can still inhabit a text comparison inside the Authored arm. TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: every grammar-emitted label is minted Structural -- each language's grammar fold mints ProductionEdge for its productions and the parse-projection roster is Core -- so no Authored label is grammar-emitted and no reader compares a grammar label by text.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.edge_label.structural_label_readers", decl_name: "the_header_edges_are_metadata_and_their_spellings_are_not", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.edge_label.structural_label_readers", decl_name: "a_member_spelled_like_the_header_does_not_make_a_module_root", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.edge_label.structural_label_readers", decl_name: "a_field_spelled_like_the_where_clause_is_not_one", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.edge_label.structural_label_readers", decl_name: "a_scope_spelled_like_import_syntax_is_not_import_syntax", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.edge_label.structural_label_readers", decl_name: "an_authored_name_spelled_like_a_core_marker_is_not_the_marker", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_cast_node", decl_name: "bcn_a_foreign_label_on_a_transform_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_cast_node", decl_name: "bcn_a_loop_passes_the_resolver_gate", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_let_annotation", decl_name: "bla_bind_admits_only_its_annotation_label", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.body_cast_node", decl_name: "bcn_an_unknown_named_label_refuses_at_binding", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
